447:The once-frenzied sparrows grow calm, settling peacefully onto the floor one by one.
448:Phew... All done! Heh heh, never doubt the Witch of Justice.
449:...So, what actually happened here?
451:I tried to catch him to figure out what was wrong, but he flew off...
452:While searching for him, I noticed that all the other sparrows in the neighborhood were acting just as crazy.
453:To make sure no innocent people got hurt, I gathered them all here and tried to calm them down with magic.
455:(Look at her catching her breath)
457:(Notice the feathers stuck in her hair)
459:Doesn't exactly look like it was nothing to me...
460:Argh-gh... J-just look at this!
461:What is this...?
463:There's definitely something evil behind this.
464:And according to the Red Panda Squad, other animals in One Han City have been acting restless too. This can only mean one thing...
466:That's so terrifying!!
467:Ah, another day, another crisis in One Han City.
468:Don't worry! With me around, everything's gonna be fine. I'll track down Piji and save all the animals!
469:So this is what it feels like to have the Witch of Justice looking out for you... How reassuring.
471:Why is that?
472:Just think about it. Evil magic must be dealt with quietly using justice magic! If we panic the citizens, the mastermind will just get smug and escalate the whole thing.
473:As the Witch of Justice, I have to nip any threat of chaos, war, or apocalypse right in the bud!
474:You're already planning for world-ending threats?!
475:Setting all that cosmic drama aside...
476:Did you skip class again today?
477:Everyone's going to worry about you, you know.
478:W-worry about me?
480:...Still, causing distress to the people around me isn't very witch-of-justice-like either.
481:Fine, I'll write an apology letter to my teacher.
482:But can you keep this just between us for now, {var:player_nickname}?
483:Deal. But on one condition.
484:A-argh! Taking advantage of a witch in a tight spot like this...
485:I'm joining the investigation with you.
486:Is the age on your student ID actually real?
487:Argh... Knowing how clingy you are, {var:player_nickname}, I can't say I'm surprised.
489:And here I thought you'd say something kinda cool, like "I want to come with you and help investigate"...
490:...
492:In that case, let's go with that condition.
493:...Hmph, you sure change your mind easily. Fine, given your dedication to defending justice...
494:For safety's sake, you'll follow my orders from here on out. Got it?
495:You got it, Captain.
496:After ensuring she officially took the day off, we set out on our investigation.
497:The park is in absolute chaos – dogs are barking frantically, cats are hissing, and their owners can barely keep them under control.
499:A huge flock of seagulls swarms a nearby diner, fighting over a fresh batch of fries.
502:Sara
503:Oh my goodness, thank you so much! The animals have been acting strangely for days now... Even Ciri, who knows them better than anyone, couldn't figure out what was wrong...
504:Don't mention it! I'm just glad my magic worked on them.
505:Perfect! We'll just keep calming the animals down like this until we find the source of this great crisis and defeat the evil final boss –
506:Following the scent of the pollen, we put out one animal disturbance after another across One Han City. Yet despite our progress, Yuzu doesn't look relieved in the slightest...
507:(Hand her a bottle of water)
508:Nice work out there. Let's rest for a bit.
509:...Thanks.
510:You know... you've been calling this a "great crisis" since the beginning. Could it be that...
511:...this is your first time handling something this big on your own?
512:...you're feeling a bit nervous?
513:!!
514:N-no way!//nI might still be an apprentice witch, but I already know tons of advanced spells!
515:It's just...
516:...things are way worse than I originally thought.
517:The animals are losing control because this pollen is draining their life force.
518:I have no idea how long this has been going on!
519:And on top of that...
521:...That really is serious. Who would do something like this to innocent animals?
522:Exactly! It's unforgivable!!
523:{var:player_nickname}, you know, all my animal friends always tell me how happy they are to live in One Han City.
524:They can't speak human language, but they're doing their part to keep our city peaceful in their own little ways.
525:Like the bees tending to the flowers, the ants quietly keeping the soil healthy, and Piji...
526:Sparrow
528:Of course I can! I'm Yuzu, the Witch of Justice!
530:Hmm... Even though the road was full of traffic, you kept circling right above that open manhole to warn people. You're so brave! How about I call you Piji the Brave?
531:Piji the Brave
533:In that case, Yuzu, Witch of Justice, I'll be your official Justice Informant from now on... Wait, no, not just me! My whole family will be your Justice Informants! We'll protect One Han City together!
534:Argh... I'm really worried about Piji.
535:He's got it the worst. He became so aggressive that he even attacked me, and my soothing spell didn't work either.
536:We still haven't found him. What if he gets hurt? Or loses control and attacks someone else, and people start thinking he's just a bad bird?!
538:(Gently pat her on the head)
539:We'll figure something out. Together.
540:T-together...?
541:Yeah, you and me.
542:Should we reach out to Kaavi, and your master Leia?
543:Truth is, as soon as I noticed something was wrong, I tried calling Master and that fortune-telling fraud... but neither of them answered.
544:Huh?
545:Argh. We witches train under a master, but every witch follows her own code.//nMy code, Kaavi's code, and Master's code are all completely different.
546:My code is Justice. But I can't force other witches to abide by my principles.
547:That's the way of witches. Master made that very clear.
548:I see.
549:Still, just because they follow different codes doesn't mean they'd stand by and let evil go unchecked, right?
550:I know Kaavi from her fortune-telling, but I haven't met Leia yet. You said she came to One Han City too. Is her magic really that powerful?
551:Argh-argh... What I said about Master still stands. You really shouldn't get too curious about her.
552:She's dangerous. And besides, this time...
553:Hm?
554:Never mind... It's probably just my imagination.
555:Alright, enough dwelling! We don't have time to waste!
556:We need to deal with the crisis in front of us first.//nAs for the next spot where lots of animals gather... there's only one place left –
557:The zoo!
