770:After hours of working alongside the Red Panda Squad, I finally manage to calm the rest of the agitated animals around the zoo.
771:As dusk settles over the city, Yuzu is nowhere to be seen, and none of my calls are going through.
772:An unknown number...? Hello?
773:Hello. Is this {var:player_nickname}?
774:Speaking. Who's calling?
776:Could I trouble you to come by? I'll send over the address.
777:Is she alright?!
778:...She is alright, just... asleep.
779:Huh?
780:Excuse me...
781:Heh, you made it. Do come in.
782:Leia sits poised at the table with effortless elegance.
783:Across the room, Yuzu lies curled up on the sofa beneath a plush blanket, fast asleep. Her staff lies on the floor beside her.
784:What on earth happened here...?
785:Nothing to worry about, really. She tracked the trail all the way here on her own, ran out of magic, and simply passed out.
786:Though she seems to have misjudged a few things... For an apprentice witch lacking real field experience, coming this far is quite an achievement. Naturally, she couldn't have done it without your constant support.
787:Out of magic...?
788:Judging by the signs of a struggle throughout the room, there was clearly more to Yuzu's magical exhaustion than Leia was letting on.
789:And what about the animal rampage?
790:Someone else has taken over the matter. Everything will be fine. Whatever comes next is far beyond what an apprentice witch needs to concern herself with.
791:Heh, it seems you have a few questions for me as well? No matter. The truth always finds a way to surface eventually.//nWe'll have plenty of opportunities to get acquainted in the future, and you'll come to understand me in time.
792:Thank you for all your help today. Now, could I trouble you to take her home? I'm afraid I'm not equipped to accommodate overnight guests.
793:Before I can press her any further,//n//nLeia sees us out.
794:In the days that follow,//n//nnews reports confirm that the animals of One Han City have returned to normal,//n//nwith no further strange incidents occurring.
795:And so,//n//nwithout us ever knowing the truth,//n//nthe so-called "Great One Han City Crisis"//n//ncomes to an unexpected close.
797:Having completely exhausted her magic, Yuzu fell into such a deep sleep that even the blaring of her alarm couldn't wake her the next morning.
